# Tax Intake Platform — Core Rules

## What this project is
A multi-tenant SaaS platform for small CPA firms to automate tax document intake.
CPAs manage clients, collect documents via portal or email, extract data with AI, export to CSV.

**Stack:** Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript + Supabase + Tailwind + shadcn/ui + Vercel

## Project structure
```
app/
  (auth)/          # CPA login/signup
  (cpa)/           # CPA dashboard — protected routes
  (client)/        # Client portal — OTP access
  api/             # API routes
components/
  ui/              # shadcn/ui components
  cpa/             # CPA-specific components
  client/          # Client portal components
lib/
  supabase/        # All DB queries go here — never inline
  claude/          # Claude API helpers
  email/           # Resend + Gmail/Outlook helpers
types/             # TypeScript types
supabase/
  migrations/      # SQL migrations
```

## TypeScript rules
- Strict mode always on — zero `any` types
- All shared types live in `/types/`
- Validate all user input with `zod`

## Component rules
- Server components by default
- `'use client'` only when you need interactivity (useState, useEffect, event handlers)
- Never fetch data in client components — use server actions or pass as props

```tsx
// ✅ Server component (default)
export default async function ClientsPage() {
  const clients = await getClients(firmId)
  return <ClientList clients={clients} />
}

// ✅ Client component (only for interactivity)
'use client'
export function ClientList({ clients }: { clients: Client[] }) {
  const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string | null>(null)
}
```

## Error handling
- API routes return `{ error: string, code: string }` on failure
- Never expose raw DB errors to frontend
- Always show loading + error states in UI

## Styling
- Tailwind utility classes only
- shadcn/ui for all UI components — never build from scratch what shadcn has
- Mobile-responsive — minimum 375px width

## What NOT to do
- No `localStorage` or `sessionStorage` for sensitive data
- No `SELECT *` — always specify columns
- No hardcoded IDs or secrets
- No `.env.local` committed to git
- No inline Supabase queries in components — always use `/lib/supabase/` helpers
